#: ../../source/reference/configuration/env_variables.md:41
msgid ""
"Note the two singulars. `FREEPORTS_DEV_TARGET_LIST` and "
"`FREEPORTS_VALIDATE_SOURCE` feed settings that are lists, and neither is "
"ever split — see the rule at the foot of this page, which they both "
"follow for the same reason."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/env_variables.md:45
msgid "Rules of the environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/env_variables.md:46
msgid "**An absent variable leaves its option unset**, and is never an error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/env_variables.md:48
msgid ""
"**Setting both `FREEPORTS_REPORTS` and one of the singular variables is "
"an error.** One of the two would have to win silently, and an override "
"nobody can see is worse than a refusal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/env_variables.md:51
msgid ""
"**A variable whose value is not valid UTF-8 is ignored with a warning**, "
"rather than failing the run — it is almost always an accident of the "
"shell rather than an intention."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/env_variables.md:54
msgid "The grammars the variables accept"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/env_variables.md:55
msgid ""
"**Booleans** — `FREEPORTS_SEPARATE_OUT`, `FREEPORTS_ARCHIVE`, "
"`FREEPORTS_SAVE_PDF` — accept, case insensitively:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/env_variables.md
msgid "True"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/env_variables.md
msgid "False"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/env_variables.md
msgid "`true`, `yes`, `1`, `y`, `t`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/env_variables.md
msgid "`false`, `no`, `0`, `n`, `f`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/env_variables.md:62
msgid ""
"Anything else is a typed error naming the variable. This is deliberately "
"more permissive than YAML's own booleans: an environment variable is "
"often set by a shell script from a value that came from somewhere else, "
"and `1` is a perfectly ordinary way to write true there."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/env_variables.md:66
msgid ""
"**Parallelism** — the three variables share one grammar, a positive "
"integer or `auto`, and differ only in the name that appears in the error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/env_variables.md:69
msgid ""
"**Verbosity** — the variant name, case-insensitively: `silent`, `error`, "
"`warn`, `info`, `debug`, `trace`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/env_variables.md:72
msgid "**Profile** — `regular`, `single_file`, `structured`, case-insensitively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/env_variables.md:74
msgid ""
"**Several documents** in `FREEPORTS_REPORTS` are separated by a pipe, `|`"
" — the same separator a batch cell uses, and one constant in the code "
"rather than two literals that could drift apart."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/env_variables.md:77
msgid "A list variable is never split"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/env_variables.md:78
msgid ""
"`FREEPORTS_TARGET_LIST` becomes a **one-element** list holding the whole "
"raw value, whatever is in it. A name containing a comma, or a pipe, still"
" names one list. To use several lists, use a source that has a list type "
"— the command line, or the YAML file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/configuration/env_variables.md:82
msgid ""
"`FREEPORTS_DEV_TARGET_LIST` and `FREEPORTS_VALIDATE_SOURCE` follow the "
"same rule, and the second is the clearest case for it: every separator "
"one might pick — comma, colon, space, semicolon — is a legal character in"
" a URI or a path, so splitting would turn one source the user meant into "
"two that do not exist."
msgstr ""

